Change: Allow managed installations to disable automatic scans on file-cache misses

The filesystem_scan_on_cache_miss option defaults to true, preserving automatic
discovery. Managed installations where all file changes go through ownCloud can
set it to false to avoid rediscovering deleted files through stale filesystem
lookups. Files added outside ownCloud, including on external storage, then need
an explicit occ files:scan.

Storage-root initialization, incomplete cached entries and watcher updates keep
their existing behaviour. The option is independent of filesystem_check_changes
and does not change or fix NFS caching itself.
